Z||000000||bHooper||07-28-2000||01:21 PM||||while i was out to lunch (in my 86 GT) i noticed that the temp gauge seemed to bounce around a little.  the car was running around 220 degree's and it seems that the needle would "bounce" while driving... particularly if i hit a small bump.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>i have never noticed this b4... any clue's?<P>p.s.<BR>since reinstalling the tranny (in may), i have not had the radiator flushed.  it lost a lot of fluid while in "surgury", so there is not much of the old fluid left (from b4 the car broke in '96)... yes, i did put new antifreeze in!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||07-28-2000||03:02 PM||||Sounds like an air pocket to me. Let the car cool down and see if the coolant is at the level of the thermostat cap. Doesn't take much air to make the gauge do what you're describing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||07-29-2000||01:40 AM||||The temp gage needle could be loose on the gage shaft too. To verify you could drive car until is is warmed up then make a sharp hard turn (left or right or both) and see if the needle moves the direction of the turn. If it does the needle needs to be fixed.||||reg||1
